    "updated_at": "2026-01-02T18:25:21Z",
    "body": "Then perhaps it would be better to replace both conditions (the one that states that the attribute lists' sizes are equal, and the one quoted in the bug description) with just one: \"There is a one-to-one correspondence between A's attributes and B's attributes such that corresponding attributes are equal.\"\n\nCurrent definition is also awkward because part of it is in the list that switches on the A's interface and part of it is underneath, even though it is also specific to a particular interface.",
